 """Option B, Step 6. Pick the tasks by program, with a seed.
 
 What this tool does, in plain words:
+- Plan v1.1: a passage and form may have up to one surviving candidate per writer pass (p1, p2, p3).
+  Before the pair rule, the survivors of each passage and form are reduced to ONE question: the
+  surviving candidate of the lowest pass (p1 before p2 before p3). The others are logged as dropped with
+  the reason LATER_PASS_NOT_NEEDED. Each kept task records which pass supplied it (pass_used).
 - Per passage it keeps at most two role-step questions. They must have different forms and
   different right things (the looser word test of tools/verdict.py). Different types are preferred.
   A second LAND question needs two agreed ^4 entries. The choice is drawn with a seed.
